rectangle "@chrislyons-dev/flarelette-crypto\n<size:10>[Container: Service]</size>" <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto>> {
  rectangle "==src.encryptDoc\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nEncrypt plaintext with a channel key. The channel key (masterKey) is never serialised by this function — it is the caller's responsibility to keep it in memory only and distribute it via encapsulateChannelKey(). Any byte sequence (document, metadata blob, message body) can be encrypted as a single call; encrypt metadata and content together in a single plaintext rather than separately." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcencryptDoc>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcencryptDoc
  rectangle "==src.decryptDoc\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nDecrypt a document encrypted by encryptDoc(). Verifies the HMAC-SHA512 MAC in constant time before attempting decryption. Throws immediately on MAC failure — no partial decryption, no timing oracle." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcdecryptDoc>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcdecryptDoc
  rectangle "==src.generateChannelKeypairs\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nGenerate a hybrid ML-KEM-1024 + X25519 keypair. Both key types are generated with cryptographically random seeds. Returns an opaque ChannelKeypairs handle — internal key bytes are not accessible to application code. Use getPublicKey() to obtain the shareable public portion and wrapKeyBundle() to persist the full keypair." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcgenerateChannelKeypairs>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcgenerateChannelKeypairs
  rectangle "==src.getPublicKey\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nExtract the public portion of a keypair for sharing with recipients. The returned ChannelPublicKey is safe to share out-of-band (Signal, QR code, etc.). It contains only public key material — no secret key bytes." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcgetPublicKey>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcgetPublicKey
  rectangle "==src.hybridEncapsulate\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>" <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srchybridEncapsulate>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srchybridEncapsulate
  rectangle "==src.hybridDecapsulate\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>" <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srchybridDecapsulate>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srchybridDecapsulate
  rectangle "==src.exportPublicBundle\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nSerialize the public portion of a keypair to a compact, shareable string. The returned string is safe to share over any channel (Signal, QR code, paste into a form). It contains only public key material." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcexportPublicBundle>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcexportPublicBundle
  rectangle "==src.importPublicBundle\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nDeserialize a public bundle string to a ChannelPublicKey. Validates the prefix and byte length. Throws on any malformed input — never returns a partial or zero-initialized key." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcimportPublicBundle>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcimportPublicBundle
  rectangle "==src.serializeKeypairs\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>" <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcserializeKeypairs>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcserializeKeypairs
  rectangle "==src.deserializeKeypairs\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>" <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcdeserializeKeypairs>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcdeserializeKeypairs
  rectangle "==src.wrapKeyBundle\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nEncrypt a keypair bundle with a wrapping key. The wrapping key is used as IKM for HKDF — it must be at least 32 bytes. Typically derived from a user passphrase (Argon2id/scrypt) or from another key exchange. Do not use a low-entropy string directly. Returns a JSON-serialisable object — all byte fields are base64url strings." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcwrapKeyBundle>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcwrapKeyBundle
  rectangle "==src.unwrapKeyBundle\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nDecrypt a keypair bundle produced by wrapKeyBundle(). Verifies the HMAC-SHA512 MAC in constant time before attempting decryption. Throws on MAC failure, wrong key, or any corrupt data — never returns a partially recovered keypair." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcunwrapKeyBundle>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcunwrapKeyBundle
  rectangle "==src.openMemoryStore\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nIn-memory KeyStore backed by a Map. Stores the opaque ChannelKeypairs handle directly — no serialization overhead. Use in Node.js, Cloudflare Workers, and tests. Data does not persist across process restarts." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcopenMemoryStore>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcopenMemoryStore
  rectangle "==src.openIndexedDBStore\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nIndexedDB-backed KeyStore. Serializes keypairs to 4,800-byte ArrayBuffers and stores them in an IndexedDB object store. Data persists across page reloads. Uses lazy connection initialisation — the DB is opened on first use and the connection is reused for subsequent operations. Object store name: 'keypairs' DB version: 1" <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcopenIndexedDBStore>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcopenIndexedDBStore
  rectangle "==src.openKeyStore\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nOpen the best available KeyStore for the current environment. Returns an IndexedDB store if `indexedDB` is available (browsers), or a memory store (Node.js, Cloudflare Workers)." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcopenKeyStore>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcopenKeyStore
  rectangle "==src.toArrayBuffer\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nConvert a Uint8Array to a plain ArrayBuffer. Web Crypto requires ArrayBuffer (not ArrayBufferLike) for all key and data parameters. Noble functions return Uint8Array<ArrayBufferLike>, which may be backed by a SharedArrayBuffer. This ensures we always pass a plain ArrayBuffer to satisfy both the DOM types and runtime requirements." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srctoArrayBuffer>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srctoArrayBuffer
  rectangle "==src.importAesKey\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>" <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcimportAesKey>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcimportAesKey
  rectangle "==src.aesGcmEncrypt\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nAES-256-GCM encrypt. Returns ciphertext with the 16-byte GCM auth tag appended. The caller is responsible for generating a unique 12-byte IV per encryption. Reusing an IV with the same key is catastrophic — this function does not enforce uniqueness; callers must generate IVs via randomIv()." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcaesGcmEncrypt>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcaesGcmEncrypt
  rectangle "==src.aesGcmDecrypt\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nAES-256-GCM decrypt. Throws if the GCM auth tag is invalid. This is a secondary authentication check; callers should validate the outer HMAC-SHA512 MAC before calling this." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcaesGcmDecrypt>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcaesGcmDecrypt
  rectangle "==src.hmacSha512\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nCompute HMAC-SHA512. Used as the outer MAC in Encrypt-then-MAC. The message should include both the nonce and the ciphertext to prevent nonce-swapping attacks." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srchmacSha512>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srchmacSha512
  rectangle "==src.constantTimeEqual\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nConstant-time byte equality check. Always use this — not ===, not a manual loop — when comparing MACs or secrets. Timing-safe comparison prevents MAC oracle attacks." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcconstantTimeEqual>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcconstantTimeEqual
  rectangle "==src.randomIv\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nGenerate a cryptographically random 12-byte IV for AES-GCM." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcrandomIv>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcrandomIv
  rectangle "==src.concatBytes\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nConcatenate Uint8Arrays into a single Uint8Array." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcconcatBytes>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcconcatBytes
  rectangle "==src._getKeypairInternal\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>" <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.src_getKeypairInternal>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.src_getKeypairInternal
  rectangle "==src.ChannelKeypairs\n<size:10>[Component: class]</size>\n\nAn opaque handle wrapping a hybrid ML-KEM-1024 + X25519 keypair. Create via generateChannelKeypairs(). Persist via wrapKeyBundle()/unwrapKeyBundle(). Do not inspect or construct directly — internal layout is not guaranteed." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcChannelKeypairs>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcChannelKeypairs
  rectangle "==src.generateChannelKey\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nGenerate a random 32-byte channel key. Pass this to encapsulateChannelKey() for each channel member, then use it with encryptDoc() to encrypt documents. Keep it in memory only — never serialise it. To add a new member later, call encapsulateChannelKey() again with the same key." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcgenerateChannelKey>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcgenerateChannelKey
  rectangle "==src.encapsulateChannelKey\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nWrap a channel key for one recipient using hybrid ML-KEM-1024 + X25519. Security properties: - Channel binding: a returned ChannelEncapsulation is only valid for the given channelId. - Recipient binding: only the holder of the matching ChannelKeypairs secret key can recover the channel key via decapsulateChannelKey(). - Forward secrecy (classical): ephemeral X25519 key is discarded after encapsulation." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcencapsulateChannelKey>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcencapsulateChannelKey
  rectangle "==src.decapsulateChannelKey\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nRecover a channel key from a ChannelEncapsulation using the recipient's secret key. Verifies channel binding — decapsulation fails if the channelId does not match the one used during encapsulateChannelKey(). This is enforced cryptographically via the HKDF info parameter: a mismatched channelId produces a different wrap key, causing AES-GCM decryption to fail." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcdecapsulateChannelKey>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcdecapsulateChannelKey
  rectangle "==src.base64urlEncode\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nBase64url encode / decode. Uses btoa/atob — available in browsers, Cloudflare Workers, and Node.js 20+. No imports, no dependencies." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcbase64urlEncode>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcbase64urlEncode
  rectangle "==src.base64urlDecode\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nDecode a base64url string to bytes. Accepts strings with or without padding. Throws on non-base64url characters." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcbase64urlDecode>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcbase64urlDecode
  rectangle "==src.deriveKey\n<size:10>[Component: function]</size>\n\nDerive a key using HKDF-SHA512." <<flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcderiveKey>> as flarelettecrypto.chrislyonsdevflarelettecrypto.srcderiveKey
}

